Jack Riggs wrote:
>
> > You can collect between 20 and 50 +0 daggers in the mines.
> > Carrying 60 daggers is a bit much, but you can stash them.
>
> Thats going to burden me out though?

No.  Only carry a dozen or so.  Not enough to become burdened.
Keep the rest in your stash.  But when you enchant your pile
of daggers, go back to your stash and carry them all at once
so they are all enchanted together.  Keep the rest in your
stash because if you hurry in combat you will misplace daggers
every once in a while.

My most recent character carried 15 blessed +6 eleven daggers
in the quiver, 5 more in the bag of holding, and 21 more in
a chest in the stash.  But all 41 were wielded together when
enchanting them.

> Cut down my inventory?

No.  They will all stack together as long as they all have the
same b/u/c and enchantment.  Taking inventory slots is only
when you first gather them not for after you have a stack of
them.

> - Spells...? not until I get a good one?

Practice any spells based on skill class.

> - Daggers definetly beat crossbow?

Daggers can be quivered and you still wield your good sword.
A crossbow must be wielded to use crossbow bolts.

When thrown daggers never disappear.  When fired crowbow
bolts somethings go away.

The supply of daggers grows slowly over time.  Since there
are now crossbow traps in the game, the supply of crossbow
bolts never grows to match their use.

